course: dictionary
lesson: 4488
title: Hatchlings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hatchling is a baby animal that has just come out of its egg. The word comes from «hatch», which means the young breaks out of the egg. Birds, turtles, snakes and crocodiles can all have hatchlings.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Turtle hatchlings climb out of their nests at night and head for the brightest horizon» tells you they are new, because they are coming out of nests, and that they are small enough to need guiding. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A baby that has just hatched.
explain: Context can also show you what a word does. «Crocodiles lay eggs in nests; the mother guards them and carries the hatchlings to water in her mouth.» The hatchlings are the newborns in the nest, not the eggs and not the grown-up crocodiles.
fact: A hatchling is a newborn animal that has just come out of its egg.
fact: «Hatch» is the action: the young breaks out of the egg.
fact: Birds, turtles, snakes and crocodiles all have hatchlings.
fact: In sea turtles and crocodiles, the warmth of the nest decides whether the babies become male or female.
fact: Warmer sand gives more girl hatchlings, and cooler sand gives more boys.
exercise: Which animal is a hatchling? | A bird's nest made of twigs | *A baby turtle that has just come out of its egg | An egg that has not cracked yet | An adult crocodile resting on a riverbank
exercise: «Sea turtle hatchlings crawl to the ocean at night, guided by moonlight. Beach lights can confuse them.» What does confuse mean here? | Turn them into adults | *Make them go the wrong way | Help them find the sea more quickly | Make them sleep all day
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the newborn animal in «Hatch is when the young breaks out of the egg.» | *hatchling | nest | horizon | sand
test: What does the mother crocodile do with the hatchlings? | Eats them | Buries them in the sand | *Guards them and carries them to water in her mouth | Leaves them alone at once
test: Why can bright beach lights be a problem for sea turtle hatchlings? | They help the hatchlings find food | They make the sand too cold | *They can lead the hatchlings the wrong way, away from the sea | They make the hatchlings grow faster
exam: What is the difference between hatch and hatchling? | They mean exactly the same thing | Hatch is a nest, and a hatchling is a kind of sea | *Hatch is the breaking out of the egg, and a hatchling is the newborn that does it | Hatch means old, and a hatchling is an adult
